{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For as yet you do not fear, etc.</b> Rashi explained: you do not yet fear. It was necessary to say this to him specifically at the removal of this plague, because Pharaoh asked only for the removal of the thunder and the hail, as it says: ״וְרַב מִהְיוֹת קֹלֹת אֱלֹהִים וּבָרָד״ (Exodus 9:28). But concerning the rain he did not say that it should cease, because the land of Egypt needs rain more than the other lands. And so Moses promised him, as it says: ״הַקֹּלוֹת יֶחְדָּלוּן וְהַבָּרָד לֹא יִהְיֶה עוֹד״ (Exodus 9:29). But in the end it was not so, but rather: ״וַיֶּחְדְּלוּ הַקֹּלוֹת וְהַבָּרָד וּמָטָר לֹא נִתַּךְ אָרְצָה״ (Exodus 9:33). And Moses was concerned lest Pharaoh hold him false and say that this was not what he had promised. Therefore Moses said: if I had known that from this day forward you would be one who fears Elohim, I would have done all your desire, for the Holy One, blessed be He — ״רְצוֹן יְרֵאָיו יַעֲשֶׂה״ (Psalms 145:19). But I know that as yet you do not fear HaShem with a whole heart; therefore HaShem will not fulfill all your desire, so that the sinner not be rewarded. Therefore everything will cease at once and there will be no rain, for He gives only to those who fear HaShem, as it is written (Jeremiah 5:24): ״וְלֹא אָמְרוּ בִלְבָבָם נִירָא נָא אֶת ה׳ אֱלֹהֵינוּ הַנֹּתֵן גֶּשֶׁם יוֹרֶה וּמַלְקוֹשׁ בְּעִתּוֹ״, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:18:48.480015845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}